        _e("kv_oauth_flows", "OAuth 2.0 Flows", "security", "# Authorization Code Flow (most common for web apps)\n1. User clicks 'Login with Google'\n2. Redirect: GET https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth?client_id=X&redirect_uri=Y&scope=email+profile&response_type=code\n3. User authenticates and consents\n4. Redirect back: GET /callback?code=AUTH_CODE\n5. Server exchanges code for tokens:\n   POST https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token\n   { client_id, client_secret, code, redirect_uri, grant_type: 'authorization_code' }\n6. Receive: { access_token, refresh_token, id_token, expires_in }\n7. Use access_token to call APIs\n\n# PKCE Flow (mobile/SPA — no client_secret)\nSame as above but with code_verifier + code_challenge\n\n# Client Credentials (machine-to-machine)\nPOST /token { client_id, client_secret, grant_type: 'client_credentials' }\n\n# Refresh tokens\nPOST /token { refresh_token, grant_type: 'refresh_token' }\n\n# JWT: { header }.{ payload }.{ signature } — base64 encoded\npayload: { sub, iat, exp, iss, aud, ... }", ["security","oauth","jwt","auth","pkce","tokens"]),
